{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>When he speaks</b> — the hater speaks entreaties; do not trust him," "<b>For seven abominations</b> — that HaShem abhors them. They are in his heart to do them, and they are those mentioned above in the verse 'six are there.' And hatred is covered in the hater's heart on account of the clamor that will come upon him; he covers and conceals the hatred, for then his evil, decreed upon him, is revealed in the midst of the assembly openly. And the proverb: he who digs a pit — in it he falls; and he who rolls stones to strike another — upon him they return, for HaShem returns them to him by means of another, and he is struck by them."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The lemma וכי in comment 0 appears to introduce only the words 'ידבר תחנונים' from the verse; the clause 'השונא אל תאמן בו' is Ibn Ezra's own paraphrase completing the sense."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:58.335082390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}